255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 178 0 R
/T (Foreign information manipulation and interference \(FIMI\), defined as coordinated efforts to manipulate information environments, distort public debate, and influence political outcomes through deceptive or inauthentic means, is conventionally studied in the context of elections in Europe and North America.[1][2] Within this literature, emphasis is frequently placed on mass audiences, voter behaviour, and the amplification of false or misleading content at scale. )
/E (Foreign information manipulation and interference \(FIMI\), defined as coordinated efforts to manipulate information environments, distort public debate, and influence political outcomes through deceptive or inauthentic means, is conventionally studied in the context of elections in Europe and North America.[1][2] Within this literature, emphasis is frequently placed on mass audiences, voter behaviour, and the amplification of false or misleading content at scale. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2 443 0 R 4 444 0 R 7]
>>
endobj
