258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 178 0 R
/T (The case documented here differs in ways that are both analytically significant and, we argue, increasingly typical. It concerns information manipulation deployed within an active interstate conflict, in a region where platform trust and safety investment is limited, fact-checking capacity is overwhelmed, and the primary audience is not a voting public but the small set of institutions whose decisions determine the cost of military aggression. This is FIMI as a component of war-fighting, and the Great Lakes region is one of its least monitored theatres.)
/E (The case documented here differs in ways that are both analytically significant and, we argue, increasingly typical. It concerns information manipulation deployed within an active interstate conflict, in a region where platform trust and safety investment is limited, fact-checking capacity is overwhelmed, and the primary audience is not a voting public but the small set of institutions whose decisions determine the cost of military aggression. This is FIMI as a component of war-fighting, and the Great Lakes region is one of its least monitored theatres.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 178 0 R
/T (This report does not document the first pro-Rwanda influence operation on record. Rather, it adds a behaviourally evidenced case to a growing body of documented activity. The prior work was the June 2024 report by the Clemson University Media Forensics Hub, which identified an AI-enabled, RPF-aligned coordinated network of at least 464 accounts on X that produced more than 650,000 posts from January 2024 onward, with the DRC conflict as its dominant content theme. That study established the scale and persistence of pro-Rwanda networked activity within the platform environment.)
/E (This report does not document the first pro-Rwanda influence operation on record. Rather, it adds a behaviourally evidenced case to a growing body of documented activity. The prior work was the June 2024 report by the Clemson University Media Forensics Hub, which identified an AI-enabled, RPF-aligned coordinated network of at least 464 accounts on X that produced more than 650,000 posts from January 2024 onward, with the DRC conflict as its dominant content theme. That study established the scale and persistence of pro-Rwanda networked activity within the platform environment.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
