265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 179 0 R
/T (The tensions between Rwanda and the Democratic Republic of Congo are not new. Their contemporary form is rooted in the events of 1994. Over approximately one hundred days, an estimated 800,000 people, the majority of them Tutsi, were killed in Rwanda in one of the fastest acts of mass murder in recorded history. The Hutu militias responsible fled across the border into what was then Zaire, settling in the east, keeping their weapons and command structures intact. The armed groups that later consolidated in those eastern forests became the FDLR, a movement rooted in the same ideology that drove the genocide, recruiting across generations and financing itself through the region's mineral trade.3)
/E (The tensions between Rwanda and the Democratic Republic of Congo are not new. Their contemporary form is rooted in the events of 1994. Over approximately one hundred days, an estimated 800,000 people, the majority of them Tutsi, were killed in Rwanda in one of the fastest acts of mass murder in recorded history. The Hutu militias responsible fled across the border into what was then Zaire, settling in the east, keeping their weapons and command structures intact. The armed groups that later consolidated in those eastern forests became the FDLR, a movement rooted in the same ideology that drove the genocide, recruiting across generations and financing itself through the region's mineral trade.3)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
