/T (MATERIALS AND METHODS Data Collection The dataset was collected from X \(formerly Twitter\) under twelve predefined hashtags and keyword collection tags relating to the eastern DRC conflict. These tags were selected to capture three overlapping layers of the information environment: \(1\) general conflict discourse \(e.g., rdc, goma, m23, rwanda, fdlr, rdf\), \(2\) campaign-specific hashtags associated with anti-Tshisekedi narratives, and \(3\) tags linked to identifiable mobilisation efforts such as CongolaisTelema. This approach allows the dataset to capture both organic discussion and coordinated campaign activity within the same analytical frame. After the removal of 110 duplicate rows, the final analysed dataset contains 2,012 unique posts from 794 unique account handles published between January 2 and March 30, 2025, with 3.46 million combined views. Each record includes full text, post URL, timestamp, engagement metrics \(views, likes, retweets, replies, quotes, bookmarks\), language, and author metadata \(display name, bio, follower and following counts, declared location, verification status\).)
/E (MATERIALS AND METHODS Data Collection The dataset was collected from X \(formerly Twitter\) under twelve predefined hashtags and keyword collection tags relating to the eastern DRC conflict. These tags were selected to capture three overlapping layers of the information environment: \(1\) general conflict discourse \(e.g., rdc, goma, m23, rwanda, fdlr, rdf\), \(2\) campaign-specific hashtags associated with anti-Tshisekedi narratives, and \(3\) tags linked to identifiable mobilisation efforts such as CongolaisTelema. This approach allows the dataset to capture both organic discussion and coordinated campaign activity within the same analytical frame. After the removal of 110 duplicate rows, the final analysed dataset contains 2,012 unique posts from 794 unique account handles published between January 2 and March 30, 2025, with 3.46 million combined views. Each record includes full text, post URL, timestamp, engagement metrics \(views, likes, retweets, replies, quotes, bookmarks\), language, and author metadata \(display name, bio, follower and following counts, declared location, verification status\).)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0]
>>
