/T (This case complicates a simple model of coordinated inauthentic behaviour as necessarily networked or state-directed. It shows that a single, persistent actor using basic distribution tactics can achieve comparable or greater reach than a structured operation, provided their content is embedded in high-visibility discovery pathways. In the context of conflict-era FIMI, effectiveness is not determined solely by scale or coordination, but by the ability to insert narratives into the informational routes that real audiences already use.)
