/E (This entire operation ran during a war that displaced hundreds of thousands of people, on a platform whose trust and safety presence in the region is minimal, in an information environment where the journalists who would normally provide ground truth were being detained by the armed group whose narrative the operation amplified. Human Rights Watch documented M23's detention and intimidation of journalists and civil society activists in occupied Goma and Bukavu during precisely the weeks the network was most active, thinning the supply of independent reporting from the ground as the online campaigns intensified.)
