/Title (By January 2025, that dispute had reached a breaking point. The fall of Goma on January 27 and Bukavu on February 16 triggered the most intensive diplomatic period of the conflict: US sanctions on Rwandan and M23 officials \(February 20\), UN Security Council Resolution 2773 demanding the withdrawal of Rwandan forces \(February 21\), an EU sanctions process that stalled on February 24 and concluded on March 17 with designations of nine Rwandan and M23 figures, and a surprise meeting between Presidents Tshisekedi and Kagame in Doha on March 18, brokered by Qatar.)
