/Title (The standard instrument for rating an influence operation's impact is the Breakout Scale, developed by Ben Nimmo, which runs from Category 1 \(an operation confined to one community on a single platform\) to Category 6 \(one that forces a policy response or a call to violence\). On that scale, this network is a Category 1, and when read through the diffusion lens, the scale is built on, which looks like failure.4 This report argues that the Breakout Scale measures the wrong thing for this class of operation. The scale measures diffusion; diffusion was not the network's theory of victory. Its theory of victory was placement at decision points, and the scale has no instrument for that. As long as defenders keep using diffusion as the primary metric, operators targeting institutions get a free pass on the operations that matter most.)
/Dest [38 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1226 0 R
/Prev 1242 0 R
>>
endobj
