/Title (What this investigation documents is not that model. It is a campaign that understood, with some precision, that the relevant battlefield for this conflict had migrated. The operation analysed here did not seek mass persuasion. It targeted a narrow set of institutional decision-makers, operating in a digital environment with minimal friction, where a small number of coordinated accounts, basic scripting, and precise timing were sufficient to insert narratives directly into the communication channels of the UN, EU and the Security Council.)
/Dest [38 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1226 0 R
/Prev 1234 0 R
/Next 1242 0 R
>>
endobj
1242 0 obj
<<
/Title (That shift matters because the instincts for countering narrative manipulation were built for a different terrain. When the battleground was legacy media, the intervention point was the editor, the fact-checker, the broadcaster's standards desk. In the environment this operation exploited, none of those friction points exist. Content moves directly from operator to institutional mention feeds, at machine speed, at the precise moments calibrated to coincide with decision-making.)
/Dest [38 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1226 0 R
/Prev 1241 0 R
/Next 1235 0 R
>>
endobj
1243 0 obj
