/Title (This pattern is not unique to conflict settings. During the Ebola outbreaks in eastern DRC, accurate information about infection clusters, mortality rates, and international response efforts was selectively reframed to support narratives of external manipulation or deliberate harm, contributing to distrust of health interventions. In both cases, the mechanism is the same: factual elements are preserved, but their meaning is altered through omission and recombination.5)
/Dest [39 0 R /Fit]
